# Paper trading with the execution MEASURED on the live Stockholm server (23 Oct 2026). Use it with any model:
#
#     set -a; source realistic.env; source model.env; set +a; python taker.py
#
# (model.env last, so a model can override a value). Nothing here places a real order.
#
# What it changes against the old paper bot (which filled at the ask seen TK_DELAY after the signal):
#   - the order is decided CODE_DELAY after the signal and MATCHES MATCH_DELAY later against the book of THAT moment
#   - it is killed (no trade) when the ask ran past the pad, like a live fill-and-kill order
#   - a marketable buy is at least $1, so cheap tokens buy 20-100 shares
#   - the sale is decided HOLD after the fill is known and matches MATCH_DELAY later too
#   - stale Binance data (late updates) is dropped instead of traded on
# The numbers come from: order call 250-400 ms (taker delay ~150 ms inside), signal->order code 70 ms (23 Oct).
# 25 Oct, after the speed change (order sent in the signal's own pass): signal->order 1-8 ms; order calls 257, 394,
# 367, 410, 272 ms (median 367; ~50 ms of it network + auth), so the order meets the book ~340 ms after it is sent
# and the bot learns the result ~30 ms later. Re-measure from the live signals table as more trades come in.
TK_REAL=1
TK_CODE_DELAY=0.005
# 25 Oct 16:05 calibrated on 427 live orders (US session included): 0.8 s + TK_QUEUE=5 gives paper the same fill rate as
# live (36%) and the same outcome on 81% of orders. Live ignores this (real orders, real delays).
TK_MATCH_DELAY=0.8
TK_RESP_DELAY=0.03
# 26 Oct: fill only if the ask stays within the limit 0.3-1.6 s after the signal (live loses the orders where it runs).
# Replay of 25 Oct: Paper-D +$40.03 -> -$2.44 (-0.22 c/sh) vs live -$8.62 (-0.51 c/sh); 85% same outcome on 712 orders.
TK_SAFE_SEC=1.6
# limit = ask + 0.04 (was 0.02): with the ~340 ms taker delay, 0.02 killed most live buys on 25 Oct morning. Replay of
# 24 Oct at 0.35 s, both halves of the day: same c/share, 65-91% filled vs 46-75%, equal or more $ (latency_sweep --pad)
TK_SLIP=0.04
TK_MAX_SPREAD=0.03
BN_MAX_LAG_MS=300
# BN_SOCKETS=2        # untested on the server: two parallel Binance connections, first copy of each update wins
